data/388/qa/audit.log:14:**1. BLOCKER — `m_per_cell` is NaN; three diagnostics are silently dead.** `build_profile.py:54` harvests aisle pitch only from gaps in `10 < d < 35` pt. Store 388's pitch is ~40.7 pt (all gaps 36.4–45.6), so `_pitches` is empty → `np.median([])` → NaN. Consequences: `corridor_width.png` is a uniform gray wash (mean RGB `[185,184,184]`, R≈G everywhere) versus 659's real heat map — the sliver-corridor detector renders zero information; all 8 `narrow[].half_width_m` and both `far_snaps[].meters` are NaN; and `PATCH_MIN_M2` in `qa_checks.coverage` net 2 is disabled (`NaN < 25.0` is False), so the net born from the store-24 regression no longer behaves as calibrated. No test asserts the value is finite — `tests/test_coverage.py:35` feeds the NaN straight into the gate. Correct value is 0.1474; recomputed metrics are all sane (tightest half-width 0.74 m, ENTRANCE snap 2.30 m), so nothing is hiding behind it — but the store shipped blind. *Code fix, not applied.*
